sequenceDiagram
    autonumber

    actor Visitor
    participant Browser as Browser / React
    participant BFF as BFF (identity module)
    participant Keycloak
    participant Ratings as Ratings API

    Visitor->>Browser: Press a rating value on a game page
    Browser->>BFF: GET /auth/rating-intent/start?gameId&slug&value
    BFF->>BFF: Validate gameId and value (invalid input never starts authentication)
    alt Already authenticated
        BFF-->>Browser: 302 back to the game with the resumed selection
    else Anonymous
        BFF->>BFF: Store short-lived return context (gameId, slug, value)
        BFF-->>Browser: 302 into the established Keycloak OIDC flow
        Browser->>Keycloak: Authorization Code + PKCE
        Keycloak-->>Browser: Callback with single-use code
        Browser->>BFF: /login/oauth2/code/keycloak
        BFF->>Keycloak: Exchange code server-to-server and validate tokens
        BFF->>BFF: Bind the return context to the resolved UserId
        BFF-->>Browser: 302 back to the same game context
    end
    Browser->>BFF: GET /auth/rating-intent
    BFF-->>Browser: 200 pending value (single use) or 404
    Browser->>Ratings: PUT /api/v1/me/ratings/{gameId} + If-None-Match:* + X-CSRF-Token
    Ratings-->>Browser: Personal rating and aggregate, or a stable rejection code

    Note over Browser,Ratings: The BFF never persists a rating on callback. The browser issues the command once and never retries it
